ng-today%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/developing-today%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"## What this is\n\nThe closing inventory audit for design #3005 (\"a measurement is a plain decimal\"), issue #3006, queue task 4350. Gate verified fresh at claim: #2985, #2997, #3000, #2791, #2743 all CLOSED — the audit was unblocked.\n\nFull inventory evidence with per-file dispositions is posted on #3006. This PR carries the audit's two in-repo deliverables:\n\n## Changes\n\n- **`pm-stack/aggregator/src/clinepass-adapter.ts`** — the one missed field-form boundary the audit found: `percentUsedOf` accepted any `Number()`-parseable string for a provider percent measurement (`\"0x10\"` → 16, `\"1e2\"` → 100, `\" 51 \"` → 51). It now takes the plain-decimal field form (`aa.ts`'s `PLAIN_DECIMAL` shape; sign stays because this gate's domain admits negatives, clamped downstream). Drift now reads as not-a-reading, never a reinterpreted percent.\n- **`pm-stack/aggregator/test/clinepass-adapter.test.ts`** — probe-matrix test: hex, scientific, and padded percent strings are refused; `\"51.5\"` still reads. Targeted run on the laptop: `bun test test/clinepass-adapter.test.ts` — 18 pass, 0 fail.\n- **`pm-stack/aggregator/README.md`** — the recorded #3005 measurement grammar stated in a new \"Measurement grammar (#3005)\" section next to the #2576 ingest contract: field form, prose form, the pins (scientific refused, padding refused, grouping stripped-not-validated, typed numbers untouched), per-app copies + shared probe matrix, and the embodiment list.\n\n## Audit findings beyond this PR\n\n- **#2789 embodiment drifted (filed, not fixed here):** the #6333 re-home (b4cf60a2db) restored `meta-quota-export.mjs` with the pre-#2789 bare `num()` — the plain-decimal gate, empty-reset tolerance, and `as_of` guard were lost, and its probe tests are gone. Restoration filed as **#7880** per the audit acceptance (\"drift filed as a named follow-up\").\n- Everything else dispositioned on #3006: Phases 1–3 embodiments verified in place (aa.ts, saas-extract grouped counts, cloudflare/supabase gates); the remaining `Number(` / `\\d+` hits are dates, identifiers, ports/limits and other #2835 arguments, already-typed values with finite checks, display math, or anchored prose patterns whose failure shape for a grouped spelling is absence, never truncation.\n\n## Notes\n\n- #3005 stays open with #7880 named and linked from it as the remaining follow-up, per the audit acceptance.\n- Verification in GitHub Actions per the packet; the targeted test above was also run locally on the laptop.\n\n<!-- codesmith:footer -->\n---\n<a href=\"https://backend.blacksmith.sh/track/enable-autofix?expires=1796776561&installation_model_id=443529&pr_number=7881&ref=codesmith_pr_footer&repository=developing-today%2Fcode&return_to=https%3A%2F%2Fgithub.com%2Fdeveloping-today%2Fcode%2Fpull%2F7881&signature=40848d71ccbcf2d28e5fbe31cc02211380efcc3c21a80f253b1c18725496d2c9\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-dark.svg\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-light.svg\"><img alt=\"Autofix with [code]smith\" src=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-dark-3x.png\" width=\"190\" height=\"28\"></picture></a>\n<sup><a href=\"https://app.blacksmith.sh/developing-today/codesmith/code/pr/7881?autoLogin=true&ref=codesmith_pr_footer\">Open in [code]smith</a> · Need help on this PR? Tag <code>@codesmith-bot</code> with what you need.</sup>\n\n<!-- codesmith:autofix:disabled -->\n<!-- /codesmith:footer -->","labels":[],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2026-11-09T00:34:47Z","updated_at":"2026-11-09T01:30:23Z","closed_at":"2026-11-09T01:30:20Z","mer